desired_outcome: Refine JoyOrGenie's interface into a warm, premium personal-concierge experience that makes intent, trusted context, live progress, recommendations, and approval immediately legible without changing the product's safety boundaries

success_criteria:
  - The first viewport has a distinctive editorial composition, one dominant intent composer, and an at-a-glance context rail for location, calendar, memory, and approval safety
  - The interface uses the approved Quiet Lantern JoyUI design tokens while adding depth, responsive rhythm, subtle texture, and purposeful motion
  - Returning-user context is visible without resembling an admin dashboard or exposing sensitive details
  - Journey stages communicate real Convex state, including working, approval, completion, and failure, without decorative fake progress
  - Recommendation cards clearly compare fit, distance, time, price, evidence source, and demo-versus-live status
  - The approval surface names the exact commitment and remains visually distinct from recommendation
  - Memory remains inspectable and removable with provenance and confidence cues
  - Mobile layout keeps the composer, stage state, and approval action usable without horizontal overflow
  - Focus states, color contrast, reduced motion, semantic headings, and touch targets remain accessible
  - Existing Convex workflows, Google Calendar paths, and demo disclosures continue working unchanged

constraints:
  - Do not expose JoyUI Studio or turn the product into a generic dashboard
  - Do not add imagery unless it materially improves comprehension
  - Do not fabricate live providers, availability, bookings, or integration status
  - Do not move or weaken the exact-hash approval boundary
  - Preserve the standalone repository and ChatGPT Sites build
  - Verify with typecheck, tests, production build, and a local render

evidence:
  - JoyCLI compiles this UI refinement contract
  - Automated tests pass
  - Production Sites build succeeds
  - Local route returns HTTP 200
